# SQL's `select` after the table, without `|`: pipe into `project` (DS0153).
mode: syntax
---- query
from t select a, b
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..19
  PIPELINE@0..18
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PROJECT_OP@7..18
      IDENT@7..13 "select"
      WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@14..15
        NAME_REF@14..15
          IDENT@14..15 "a"
      COMMA@15..16 ","
      WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@17..18
        NAME_REF@17..18
          IDENT@17..18 "b"
  WHITESPACE@18..19 "\n"

error[DS0153]: `select` is SQL: DataScript pipes the table into an operator
  --> query:1:8
  |
1 | from t select a, b
  |        ^^^^^^ expected `|` before this
  |
  = help: pipe the rows into `project`: `| project`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | project a, b
which parses without errors
